<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yunus ibn Ilyas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yunus ibn Ilyas was a 9th-century ruler of the Barghawata, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> confederation on the Atlantic plains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. According to al-Bakri he openly proclaimed the religion of his grandfather <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salih-ibn-tarif">Salih ibn Tarif</a> and spread it by force, waging wars against neighbouring tribes. His reign established the Barghawata faith as the official religion of the state.</p></div>
